SUMMARY:SMC Trail Work Volunteer Day
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**TRAIL WO
 RK will continue rerouting the Hogenauer Trail** (we are making progress!)
  up the slope and away from recently installed property fences. **Meet At:
 ** Dog Park/ Wildflower Preserve\, 11 Bear Lane\, Maplewood. From there\, 
 we will walk to Crater View on Crest drive and then to the Hogenauer trail
  work site. (Note: While we normally meet the first Sudnay of each month\,
  this volunteer day was shifted after the Labor Day weekend.)\n\nTrail wor
 k is physically challenging but very satisfying as we use hand tools to bu
 ild and repair trails. Participants must be 15+ years. Those younger than 
 18 must be accompanied by an adult. Participants **should wear long pants*
 * due to [ticks](https://www.somocon.org/?page_id=193928&fb) and thron bus
 hes and sturdy shoes\, and bring gloves (though backup gloves will be avai
 lable). Tools\, water\, and a snack will be provided. (Registration is not
  required though if you sign up on Meetup\, it helps us know how many tool
 s to bring.) Only heavy\, steady rain cancels.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/315971387/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260804T045239Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260804T045239Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
